# lahn course
version 1
title Reading music
description From your first note on the staff to reading short melodies to a beat, one note at a time.
instrument guitar

unit The staff

lesson Your first note on the staff
title Five lines
text Music is written on five lines, the staff. The higher a note sits on it, the higher it sounds.
text The sign at the start is the clef. The little 8 under it says guitar sounds an octave lower than written: that's how guitar music is always written.
title E, in the top space
text The note in the space at the top of the staff is E: the thinnest string, played open. lahn shows it on the neck too.
exercise
type notes
notes E4
show staff
where yes
count 3
pass 2

lesson E and F
text F sits on the top line, just above E. It's the 1st fret of the thinnest string.
exercise
type notes
notes E4 F4
show staff
where yes
count 6
pass 5

lesson E, F and G
text G sits just above the staff, over the top line: the 3rd fret.
exercise
type notes
notes E4 F4 G4
show staff
where yes
count 8
pass 7

lesson E, F and G on your own
text Now the neck doesn't show you where: read the note, and play it. A slip shows you.
exercise
type notes
notes E4 F4 G4
show staff
count 8
pass 7

unit The B string

lesson B, on the middle line
text The middle line of the staff is B: the B string, open.
exercise
type notes
notes B3
show staff
where yes
count 3
pass 2

lesson B, C and D
text C is in the space above B (the 1st fret of the B string), D on the line above that (the 3rd fret).
exercise
type notes
notes B3 C4 D4
show staff
where yes
count 8
pass 7

lesson B, C and D on your own
exercise
type notes
notes B3 C4 D4
show staff
count 8
pass 7

unit Two strings

lesson From B to G
text All six now: B, C, D on the B string, E, F, G on the thinnest one. Up the staff, up the alphabet.
exercise
type notes
notes B3 C4 D4 E4 F4 G4
show staff
where yes
count 10
pass 8

lesson From B to G on your own
exercise
type notes
notes B3 C4 D4 E4 F4 G4
show staff
count 12
pass 10

unit To a beat

lesson Reading in time
title Now with a beat
text Until now lahn waited for you. Now the notes come on a slow beat, a note on each one: a bar of clicks counts you in.
text The same six notes, two bars at a time. When you get a pass clean, it goes a little faster.
exercise
type reading
key C
scale major
frets 0 3
strings 5 6
leap 1
cells quarter
bars 2
tempo 50 70 5
goal 1

lesson A rest now and then
text A rest is a beat with no note: let the string be quiet, and count it.
exercise
type reading
key C
scale major
frets 0 3
strings 5 6
leap 2
cells quarter rest
bars 2
tempo 50 70 5
goal 1
